\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item intensity 0 is NOT a measured zero: FlashLFQ writes a literal 0 for a peptide it did not quantify in a sample, and mzLib keeps it (QuantifiedPeptideFromTsv.cs:14). Filter on detection_type before a mean or a log.
\item retention_time is IsoTracker output only (QuantifiedPeptideFromTsv.cs:61); plain FlashLFQ and MetaMorpheus tables name it in absent_fields, and peak_order likewise.
\item Long format: offset and limit count PEPTIDES, and returned_count counts rows.
\item Many files: \code{--paths-stdin} reads the list in ONE process, \code{--threads} at a time, into one long table with source_index and source_path first. The output does not depend on \code{--threads} (a tested property); the default of 1 is a memory choice, since every reader materialises the whole file.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. For many files call \code{\link{readers_read_quantified_peptides_many}()} once rather than looping this function: one process, one start-up, and the thread count stated on the wire.
}
